{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"toadyish-sulfurous-ovenbird","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe CLI exposes 72 top-level verbs. Twenty of them duplicate an operation that already exists on a golden-path verb, fits one flag, or belongs under a storage-maintenance noun: `exists`/`format` over `resolve`; `check-ac`/`clarity-check`/`quality-check` over one `check`; `tag`/`untag` over `edit`'s existing tag flags; `get-file-impact`/`get-verify-commands` over `show --field`; `list-descendants` over `deps`; `session-logs` over `list`; `compact`/`compact-all`; and the seven tracker verbs that become `rebar store <sub>`. The operator ruled on 2026-09-06: hard cutover with no working aliases, the existing removed-name hint mechanism kept and populated so future releases stay compatible with it, every doc surface accurate, and release notes listing each old-to-new spelling. Golden-path verbs, gate verbs, CI-invoked trust verbs, and existing families keep their spellings; `reclaim-collapse` belongs to the ADR 0106 epic and is untouched. The full mapping table, usage census, and the nested-group mechanism to reuse are recorded in this epic's first comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every removed spelling exits 2 with argparse's invalid-choice error plus a hint naming the replacement, and none has a route. Checked by the parametrized dispatch test over the hint registry.\n- [ ] Every surviving operation keeps its `--output json` bytes, its exit codes, and its library and MCP names. Checked by the re-targeted goldens, the exit-code doc conformance test, and an unchanged parity manifest.\n- [ ] Committed help, the generated CLI reference, the exit-code table, AGENTS.md, the packaged guides, templates, example skills, and MCP client examples teach only the new spellings, and the release notes and a new ADR record every rename. Checked by the docs story's repo-wide grep and the ADR gates.\n- [ ] A held-out test keeps removed spellings from returning to any teaching surface and proves each hint's replacement is a live command. Checked by the red-then-green record in that story.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Ticket-verb merges story: delivers criterion 1 for the twelve ticket verbs and criterion 2 for their replacements.\n- Store group story: delivers criterion 1 for the nine storage verbs and criterion 2 for the `store` members, depends on the merges story (shared registry and hint dict).\n- Documentation story: delivers criterion 3, depends on the store group story.\n- Held-out drift test story: delivers criterion 4, depends on the documentation story.","id":"e045-84a5-e545-4f46","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Consolidate the CLI verb surface: 72 verbs to 54, hard cutover with removed-name hints"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788805764426216121,"uuid":"eef34f36-6a31-4d48-8988-50865a4390d6"}